<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-STATE STAKE IN MAAPANK TO BE SOLD.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-STATE STAKE IN MAAPANK TO BE SOLD.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The privatisation agency on Wednesday decided to sell the state's stake in small Estonian commercial banks Maapank (Land Bank) and Innovatsioonipank.</p>
<p>It will sell 179,416 shares in Maapank and 250 shares in Innoavatsioonipank, Economics Minister Jaak Leimann told a news conference.</p>
<p>The shares, which form less than two percent of the banks' share capital, will be sold in a public auction, he added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
